{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 36, :comments ["<b>And you shall make a screen.</b> A curtain — it is a screen opposite the entrance, as in ״שַׂכְתָּ בַעֲדוֹ״ (Job 1) — a term for a shield." "<b>The work of an embroiderer.</b> The figures are made in it by needlework — as the design on this side, so the design on this side." "<b>Embroiderer.</b> The name of the craftsman, not the name of the craft, and its Targum is עוֹבַד צַיָּר and not עוֹבַד צִיּוּר. The dimensions of the screen are like the dimensions of the veil — ten cubits by ten cubits."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:54:52.128128193Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}